  "reason": "1) Evidence: We have only one data point (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), which is a weak baseline. The most critical unknown is whether the image modality carries useful discriminative signal at all, since this determines whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing or whether we should focus on improving RNA representations. 2) This experiment (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly tests image informativeness by switching only the modality while keeping the profile setting (singleprofile) and using a standard, well-established encoder. It is a clean single-variable comparison against the RNA baseline. 3) With 8 experiments remaining, resolving the modality question first is the highest-value use of the next slot: if image_only substantially outperforms 48.5%, we pivot to multimodal configs; if it is comparable or worse, we invest remaining budget in RNA encoder upgrades (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design axis."
}

